      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concerns that these summits solely benefit large corporations are a common talking point, but they miss the bigger picture of global stability. These agreements actually create a level playing field by enforcing international standards that prevent predatory practices by any single powerful entity. Moreover, by opening up global markets, they provide smaller local businesses with access to massive international supply chains they could never access alone. Therefore, they are a net positive for stabilizing the entire economic ecosystem, not just the largest players.",
      "source": "target",
