      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument about national sovereignty is a deeply rooted, yet often exaggerated, fear. While treaties require adherence to certain agreed-upon frameworks, these agreements are designed to *facilitate* national prosperity, not erase it. A strong, stable global economy, built on these rules, is the very foundation upon which a nation can best protect its citizens' interests. Prioritizing isolationism over global integration is a recipe for economic stagnation and vulnerability to international shocks.",
